<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 45-50,000 T fuel oil to London firm.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 45-50,000 T fuel oil to London firm.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tupras, Turkey's state-run oil refiner, announced on Thursday that it sold 45,000 to 50,000 tonnes of fuel oil through a tender to the London-based company OMV Trading.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the tender, issued on February 19, was awarded at a premium of $4.95 per tonne.</p>
<p>The loading will be from Aliaga refinery on March 7-9, it said.</p>
<p>OMV Trading is a subsidiary of Austrian oil group OMV AG.</p>
<p>-- Ankara Newsroom +90 312 4462940</p>
</text>
